# Template. On first run this is copied to ~/.zprofile.local, which git does
# not track. Put real work-specific env vars in that copy. This file itself
# is committed to a public repo, so anything written here is published.
#
# Login shells only, once per session — a good place for secrets pulled
# from a credential helper (never store secrets in plaintext here).

# Example: a PAT pulled from `gh` for a work GitHub host, not stored in
# plaintext:
# export GITHUB_PAT_WORK="$(gh auth token -h github.example.com 2>/dev/null)"
